title: Renaissance subtract round — deleted duplicate lore-ui + graph-ui (135MB)
summary: 'The subtractive half of subtractive-then-additive. Deleted the lore-ui and graph-ui standalone Vite SPAs (~135MB) — verbatim older twins of the lore/graph sections already inside the Platform. Removed their orphaned build scripts + files-array dist entries. Repointed the bare `paradigm lore` and `paradigm graph` launchers to `paradigm serve` with the matching section (one UI entry point, UX preserved). Kept the lore-server/graph-server route handlers (the Platform sections use them) and graph.ts (graph generate needs graphGenerateCommand). Build + CLI 441 green; smoke-tested all three repointed paths live. Deferred: folding standalone sentinel/ui + university/ui (needs parity check).'
symbols_touched:
  - '#serve'
files_modified:
  - packages/paradigm/src/index.ts
  - packages/paradigm/package.json
  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - commands/graph.ts exports BOTH the retiring serve action (graphCommand) AND the live graphGenerateCommand — so 'delete the launcher' meant repoint the bare action + keep the file, not delete it. Always check what else a to-be-deleted module exports before rm.
  - 'Repointing the old per-section launchers (paradigm lore/graph) to `paradigm serve --sections X` is gentler than deleting them outright: it removes the duplicate UI STACK (the real goal, 135MB) while preserving muscle memory, and leaves exactly one UI implementation. Better than the audit''s literal ''delete the launchers''.'
  - The standalone SPAs (lore-ui/graph-ui) are distinct from the route-handler dirs (src/lore-server/src/graph-server) the Platform sections consume — deleting the former while keeping the latter is the safe cut. Name the keep/delete seam explicitly before rm -r.
